# SABOTAGE: T74 (spec §I1 CRM two-way email sync) gate sabotage — defeats the HONEST EMPTY STATE
# of the CRM mailbox settings surface. `Samen.Web.CRM.MailboxLive.load/2` assigns
# `provider_configured` from `Samen.Mailbox.provider_configured?/0` — the adapter's own answer,
# never an assumption. This patch hardcodes it to `true`, the "assume it works" lie: a host with
# NO mailbox provider wired (the CI default, and every un-adopted host) would then render
# "No mailbox connected yet." plus a live Connect affordance instead of "Mailbox sync is not
# configured." — collapsing "nothing is wired" into "connected but quiet", which is exactly the
# distinction the fail-honest contract exists to preserve. The CONFIGURED-state tests stay green
# (they wire a real provider), so the flip isolates the honesty guarantee. Reverts byte-exact.
# REGENERATED in the T74 fix round (LOW-3 added the honest connect-notice affordance to the same
# assign block, shifting this hunk's context).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_mailbox_settings_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: UNCONFIGURED: the page says so, offers NO connect affordance, and fabricates NO data
# MUST_FAIL: UNCONFIGURED even when connection ROWS exist — the provider is the source of truth
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/mailbox_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/mailbox_live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/mailbox_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/mailbox_live.ex
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@
       org_id: org_id,
       connections: Reads.mailbox_connections(mount, scope),
       # The fail-honest predicate — read from the adapter itself, never assumed.
-      provider_configured: Samen.Mailbox.provider_configured?(),
+      provider_configured: true,
       scope_mounted: not is_nil(Reads.mailbox_connection_resource(mount)),
       connect_notice: nil
     )
